cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gridpulse, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "gridpulse: robustness of carbon-optimal data-center siting to the carbon-accounting choice"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline and specification-curve (multiverse) analysis showing that
  carbon-optimal data-center siting is not robust to the carbon-accounting choice.
  Using two years of hourly EIA-930 data for 27 US balancing authorities, gridpulse
  computes a per-BA carbon factor under a multiverse of accounting choices (temporal,
  accounting boundary, spatial resolution, estimation method) and finds that 24 of 27
  balancing authorities change siting rank, with only the Pacific-Northwest hydro core
  robust across every choice. Version 1.0.0 turns the result into a constructive
  decision rule (min-max regret over the accounting methods, whose robust site is the
  Pacific-Northwest hydro core, stable under estimation uncertainty) and adds a
  state-dependent autoregressive marginal-emissions estimator.
